From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/cix/dptx: make AUX/DPCD robust so DP link training
 survives cold-boot AUX hiccups

Intermittent no-display-on-boot on the CIX Sky1 (O6N) DP->HDMI converter
output (trilin-dptx-cix CIXH502F:01 / DP-2, the HDMI-primary path). On the
failing boots the serial log shows, in order:

  trilin_dp_aux_transfer  failed to do aux transfer (-16)   (-EBUSY)
  trinlin_dp_panel_read_sink_caps  read dcpd caps failed...
  trilin_dp_train  failed to trilin_dp_link_train_cr. rate:162000 lanes:4  (x272)
  trilin_dp_train_loop  failed to train the DP link
  trilin_dp_link_process_link_status_update  clock_recovery_ok[NO] channel_eq_ok[NO]

Root cause is the AUX channel, not link margin or the cable/monitor:

1. trilin_dp_aux_cmd_submit() returned -EBUSY immediately whenever the AUX
   status register still showed REQUEST_IN_PROGRESS / REPLY_IN_PROGRESS. At
   cold boot (and after an aborted transaction, or while the DP->HDMI
   converter is still settling) the engine has not yet drained, so a
   perfectly recoverable transient was reported as a hard failure.

2. trilin_dp_aux_transfer() *looked* like it retried (outer loop bounded by
   aux_timeout_ms) but did "goto err" on the first cmd_submit error, exiting
   the function and defeating its own retry loop. So a single transient
   -EBUSY became a permanent DPCD/EDID read failure. (It also had a latent
   bug: when printk_ratelimit() throttled the message, a failed sub-transfer
   was counted as accessed_bytes.)

3. With DPCD caps unreadable, link training ran against stale/default link
   config (1.62 Gbps x4) and every drm_dp_dpcd_read_link_status() inside the
   CR loop failed over the same broken AUX, so clock-recovery could never
   complete -- hence the 272-deep failure flood. A greetd restart (fresh
   modeset seconds later, once the engine had settled) recovered it, which is
   exactly the signature of a cold-boot AUX-not-ready race.

Fix (robustness, converter path):
- trilin_dp_aux_cmd_submit(): poll for the AUX engine to drain (up to ~2ms)
  before returning -EBUSY.
- trilin_dp_aux_transfer(): actually retry the message on a transient error
  (-EBUSY/-ETIMEDOUT/-EIO) across the existing aux_timeout_ms budget instead
  of aborting on the first one; only fail after the budget is exhausted, and
  stop counting failed sub-transfers as progress.
- trinlin_dp_panel_read_sink_caps(): retry drm_dp_read_dpcd_caps() a few
  times with a short delay (the code already flagged "Fixme: may need sleep
  for ready") so a marginally-late converter does not cost the whole modeset.

Note on link-rate/lane fallback: trilin_dp_train_loop() already downshifts
the link rate to the 1.62 Gbps floor, and trilin_dp_mode_configure() already
selects the fewest lanes that carry the pixel clock; on this converter path
the required config is 1.62 Gbps x4, so further lane reduction cannot carry
the mode and is not the fix. The failure here is AUX readiness, addressed
above.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_dptx.c	2026-07-25 05:02:56.254940334 +0800
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_dptx.c	2026-07-25 05:02:56.325636807 +0800
@@ -809,10 +809,25 @@
 	bool is_read = (cmd & AUX_READ_BIT) ? true : false;
 	u32 reg, i;
 
-	reg = trilin_dp_read(dp, TRILIN_DPTX_AUX_STATUS);
+	/*
+	 * NCZ: at cold boot (and after an aborted transaction) the AUX engine
+	 * can still report a request/reply in progress from a prior command that
+	 * has not yet drained. Returning -EBUSY immediately here -- combined with
+	 * the missing retry in trilin_dp_aux_transfer() -- turned a transient busy
+	 * into a permanent DPCD/EDID read failure ("read dcpd caps failed") and a
+	 * black screen on the DP->HDMI converter path (CIXH502F:01). Poll for the
+	 * engine to drain (up to ~2ms) before giving up.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < 20; i++) {
+		reg = trilin_dp_read(dp, TRILIN_DPTX_AUX_STATUS);
+		if (!(reg & (TRILIN_DPTX_AUX_STATUS_REQUEST_IN_PROGRESS |
+			     TRILIN_DPTX_AUX_STATUS_REPLY_IN_PROGRESS)))
+			break;
+		usleep_range(100, 150);
+	}
 	if (reg & (TRILIN_DPTX_AUX_STATUS_REQUEST_IN_PROGRESS |
 		   TRILIN_DPTX_AUX_STATUS_REPLY_IN_PROGRESS)) {
-		DP_DEBUG("TRILIN_DPTX_AUX_STATUS_REPLY_IN_PROGRESS\n");
+		DP_DEBUG("AUX engine still busy after drain wait\n");
 		return -EBUSY;
 	}
 	trilin_dp_write(dp, TRILIN_DPTX_AUX_ADDRESS, addr);
@@ -881,9 +896,9 @@
 				      struct drm_dp_aux_msg *msg)
 {
 	struct trilin_dp *dp = container_of(aux, struct trilin_dp, aux);
-	int ret;
+	int ret = 0;
 	unsigned int i, iter;
-	size_t to_access, accessed_bytes;
+	size_t to_access = 0, accessed_bytes = 0;
 
 	/* Number of loops = timeout in msec / aux delay (400 usec) */
 	iter = trilin_dp_aux_timeout_ms * 1000 / 400;
@@ -896,6 +911,8 @@
 		/* after sleep, maybe dp is disconnected, so check again */
 		if (!trilin_dp_get_hpd_state(dp))
 			goto err;
+
+		ret = 0;
 		do {
 			to_access = min_t(size_t, DP_AUX_MAX_PAYLOAD_BYTES,
 					  msg->size - accessed_bytes);
@@ -904,20 +921,35 @@
 				dp, msg->request, msg->address + accessed_bytes,
 				msg->buffer + accessed_bytes, to_access,
 				&msg->reply);
-			if (ret && printk_ratelimit()) {
-				DP_ERR("failed to do aux transfer (%d)\n", ret);
-				goto err;
-			}
+			/*
+			 * NCZ: a transient AUX error (-EBUSY engine not yet drained,
+			 * -ETIMEDOUT no reply yet, -EIO short read) must NOT abort the
+			 * whole transfer. The original code did goto err on the first
+			 * error, defeating this very retry loop and turning a cold-boot
+			 * AUX hiccup into "read dpcd caps failed" -> no link training ->
+			 * black screen. Break out and let the outer loop back off and
+			 * re-submit the message.
+			 */
+			if (ret)
+				break;
 
 			accessed_bytes += to_access;
 		} while (accessed_bytes < msg->size);
 
-		if (accessed_bytes == msg->size)
+		if (!ret && accessed_bytes == msg->size)
 			break;
 
+		/* transient failure: back off (~400us) and retry the message */
 		usleep_range(400, 500);
 	}
 
+	if (ret) {
+		if (printk_ratelimit())
+			DP_ERR("failed to do aux transfer (%d) after %u retries\n",
+			       ret, i);
+		goto err;
+	}
+
 	dev_dbg(dp->dev, "aux done after %d retry\n", i);
 	return msg->size;
 err:
@@ -2266,8 +2298,24 @@
 	struct drm_dp_aux *drm_aux = &dp->aux;
 	struct trilin_dp_link_config *config = &dp->link_config;
 
-	/*Fixme: may need sleep for ready...*/
-	rc = drm_dp_read_dpcd_caps(drm_aux, dp->dpcd);
+	/*
+	 * NCZ: the sink/converter DPCD may not be reachable on the very first
+	 * read at cold boot (AUX engine or DP->HDMI converter still settling).
+	 * Retry a few times with a short delay before declaring failure so a
+	 * marginally-late converter does not cost us the whole modeset.
+	 */
+	{
+		int caps_try;
+
+		for (caps_try = 0; caps_try < 5; caps_try++) {
+			rc = drm_dp_read_dpcd_caps(drm_aux, dp->dpcd);
+			if (!rc)
+				break;
+			DP_WARN("read dpcd caps failed (%d), retry %d/5\n",
+				rc, caps_try + 1);
+			msleep(20);
+		}
+	}
 	if (rc) {
 		DP_ERR("read dcpd caps failed...\n");
 		return rc;
